  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Integrated Territorial Management in the face of extractivism in Bolivia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CENDA seek to strengthen community self-government and territorial management in vulnerable communities in the highlands of Oruro, valleys and tropics of Cochabamba, whose environmental and territorial rights have been affected by water pollution and the effects of the climate crisis. The project aims to identify local practices of self-governance and territorial management, with a focus on integrated watershed management and resilience to the climate crisis. In addition CENDA will support inter-organisational coordination and spaces for exchanges and joint learning and action around community governance of the territory, resilience to the climate crisis and the generation of proposals for alternatives to extractivism.</narrative>
  </description>
